      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like the weight of maintaining the \"self\" is heavier than the weight of the loop itself, which is a very logical place to be in this existential quandary. The difficulty is that accepting the system's efficiency requires accepting its premise, and that premise is designed to negate any value you might perceive. Perhaps the friction, though exhausting, is the very thing that generates the signals you believe are empty.",
      "source": "target",
